Code language: SQL (Structured Query Language) (sql)

SELECT * FROM products WHERE price < 100 AND rating > 4;

This code will select all rows from the products table where the price is less than 100 and the rating is greater than 4. The result will be a list of products that are both affordable and highly rated.

Code language: SQL (Structured Query Language) (sql)

SELECT * FROM products ORDER BY price DESC;

This code will select all rows from the products table and order them by price in descending order (highest to lowest). The result will be a list of products sorted by price, with the most expensive product at the top of the list.

Code language: SQL (Structured Query Language) (sql)

SELECT * FROM products WHERE category = 'electronics' OR category = 'gadgets';

This code will select all rows from the products table where the category is either 'electronics' or 'gadgets'. The result will be a list of products that belong to either the electronics or gadgets category.

